Dear Koichi,

Before our 14:00 reading today, could you look at Ishikawa's attached v0.2 ta=
ble and help me with two points?

First, I propose putting the progress from the implementation ledger in a sep=
arate field: as of 09:00 on 20 January, initial observation has been complete=
d for 31 of the 48 planned participants. The remaining 17 have not yet been o=
bserved. How should we explain those 17 when reading the table, so that they =
are not mistaken for missing records within an item?

Second, four items have at least one missing entry among their respective eli=
gible records. I propose describing these as item-level recording status, sep=
arately from progress. The first three items are counted in participants, whi=
le the response-date item is counted in issued query rows. Could you check wh=
ether this distinction and the item-specific denominators are clear enough fo=
r the meeting material?

The attached table is KRC-LDO-20260120-TAB-001 v0.2, using the 09:00 cutoff. =
I would like to keep our description to what the records at that point suppor=
t.

Thank you, and see you this afternoon.

Best regards,
Mitsuko Suzuki
Katsuragawa Clinical Research Center

